# UI Improvements & Screen Dimmer Plan

## Context

Single-screen Expo radio app. Layout: Header → ControlPanel → CategoryTabs → StationList.
Playback via `useRadioPlayer()` / `RadioPlayerService`. Hook signal: `playerState.isPlaying`.
`expo-keep-awake` active while playing (screen stays on, playback stable on Galaxy).
Screen dimming via **in-app overlay only** — `expo-brightness` was tried and reverted.

## UI Improvement 1: Pinned Mini Player Bar ✅ DONE

**Problem:** ControlPanel scrolls off-screen when browsing the station list.

**Completed:**
- `components/MiniPlayerBar.tsx` — pinned to bottom inside `SafeAreaView`, visible when `currentStation` is set
- Shows station name, episode title (podcasts), status, play/pause, stop
- Reuses `togglePlayPause` and `stop` from `App.tsx`
- Bottom safe area via `useSafeAreaInsets()` from `react-native-safe-area-context` (required for Android `edgeToEdgeEnabled`)

**Optional later:** Expandable volume or dim-mode indicator

## UI Improvement 2: Finish i18n in ControlPanel ✅ DONE

**Problem:** ControlPanel uses hardcoded Korean (`연결 중...`, `볼륨`) while other components use `useLanguage()`.

**Completed:**
- `useLanguage()` wired into `ControlPanel.tsx`
- Loading and volume labels use `t.loading`, `t.volume`
- Play/pause/stop buttons use `t.play`, `t.pause`, `t.stop` as accessibility labels

**Follow-up (optional):** Map `RadioPlayerService` error messages through i18n in the UI layer

## Feature: Screen Dim via Overlay After 10 Seconds ✅ DONE

**Goal:** After 10 continuous seconds of playback, dim screen visually. Audio continues. Tap restores and resets timer.

**Approach:** In-app overlay only (does not change system brightness; minimal battery savings)

**Completed:**
- `hooks/useScreenDimmer.ts` — 10s timer (3s in `__DEV__`), gated on `isPlaying && !isLoading`
- `components/ScreenDimOverlay.tsx` — full-screen `rgba(0,0,0,0.7)` overlay (~30% perceived brightness)
- Transparent tap layer with hint; tap calls `wake()` to dismiss overlay
- Wired in `App.tsx`; i18n via `screenDimmedHint` (`탭하여 화면 켜기` / `Tap to wake screen`)
- `PlayerKeepAwake` active during playback — dimming and keep-awake coexist

**Note:** Overlay blocks UI interaction while dimmed; does not turn screen off.

## Behavior Matrix

| Event | Action |
|-------|--------|
| `isPlaying && !isLoading` | Start 10s timer |
| Timer fires | Show dim overlay |
| User taps | Hide overlay, restart timer if still playing |
| Pause / Stop | Clear timer, remove overlay |
| Station switch while playing | Reset timer |
| App backgrounded | Clear overlay (restart timer on foreground if still playing) |

## UI Improvement 3: Galaxy Tab Landscape Layout ✅ DONE

**Problem:** App is portrait-only; Galaxy Tab should default to landscape with a split layout.

**Completed:**
- `expo-screen-orientation` — phones lock portrait, tablets lock landscape on launch
- `utils/deviceUtils.ts` — tablet detection (shortest side ≥ 600dp)
- `hooks/useDeviceLayout.ts` — `isLandscapeTablet` for responsive layout
- `hooks/useOrientationLock.ts` — runtime orientation lock by device class
- `components/LandscapeDecorPanel.tsx` — gradient decor panel with animated wave rings when playing
- `App.tsx` — landscape tablet: radio UI in left panel (~480dp), decor fills remainder
- `app.json` orientation `"default"` + Android manifest `unspecified` (JS handles lock)

**Layout:** Left panel = Header → ControlPanel → CategoryTabs → StationList + MiniPlayerBar. Right = branded decor with now-playing card.

## Feature: Background Playback & Media Controls (Planned)

**Problem:** Playback is tied to `expo-av` + `expo-keep-awake`. Switching apps or turning the screen off is unreliable on Galaxy; no notification or lock-screen controls.

**Goal:** Play radio while using other apps. Stable background audio on Galaxy. Notification + lock-screen play/pause/stop. Optional: remove or optionize `keep-awake` after background is stable.

**Approach:** Expo prebuild/dev build (already in use via `expo run:android`). Add `react-native-track-player` — not Expo Go. Migrate `RadioPlayerService` from `expo-av` to track-player. UI (`useRadioPlayer`, ControlPanel, MiniPlayerBar) stays on the same hook interface where possible.

**Why not Expo SDK only:** `expo-av` supports `staysActiveInBackground` but lacks Foreground Service, media notification, and lock-screen Now Playing. `FOREGROUND_SERVICE` is declared in `app.json` but not wired.

### Planned steps

| # | Step | Scope |
|---|------|--------|
| 1 | Install & configure `react-native-track-player` | `package.json`, `app.json`, Android manifest, playback service entry |
| 2 | Add playback service bootstrap | `index.ts` or `services/playbackService.ts` — register remote events |
| 3 | Migrate `RadioPlayerService` | Replace `expo-av` `Audio.Sound` with track-player API; keep singleton + subscribe pattern |
| 4 | Live stream playback | Korean/international stations — `Track` with stream URL |
| 5 | Podcast playback | Episode URL, seek/progress via track-player position events |
| 6 | Media notification & lock-screen | Station title, play/pause/stop actions (track-player built-in) |
| 7 | Android permissions | `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK` (Android 14+), verify Galaxy background |
| 8 | Galaxy real-device QA | Background, screen off, station switch, phone call / audio focus |
| 9 | `keep-awake` policy | Remove default `PlayerKeepAwake` or make user-toggle after step 8 passes |
| 10 | i18n for notification labels | Optional — `locales/` for notification channel / action text if customizable |

### Behavior matrix (target)

| Event | Action |
|-------|--------|
| User leaves app while playing | Audio continues; media notification visible |
| User taps pause in notification | Pause; UI syncs via `RadioPlayerService` state |
| Screen turns off | Audio continues (no `keep-awake` required) |
| Station switch while playing | Reset track; update notification metadata |
| Network drop | Retry/reconnect logic in `RadioPlayerService` (step 8 follow-up) |

### Constraints

- **Expo Go:** not supported — use `expo run:android` / EAS build (current workflow)
- **Do not remove `keep-awake` before step 8** — previously caused Galaxy playback stop in background
- **Real device required** — emulator insufficient for Samsung background behavior

